1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,644
Most cinnamon sold around the world

2
00:00:02,644 --> 00:00:04,205
isn't true cinnamon.

3
00:00:04,735 --> 00:00:07,390
True cinnamon comes from one island:

4
00:00:07,390 --> 00:00:08,377
Sri Lanka.

5
00:00:08,907 --> 00:00:11,360
For centuries, empires fought over it:

6
00:00:11,360 --> 00:00:12,716
first the Portuguese,

7
00:00:12,716 --> 00:00:14,192
and then the Dutch.

8
00:00:14,722 --> 00:00:17,286
Today, Sri Lanka grows

9
00:00:17,286 --> 00:00:19,821
about 80–90% of it.

10
00:00:19,821 --> 00:00:23,007
Last year, exports hit a record:

11
00:00:23,007 --> 00:00:25,148
about $260 million.

12
00:00:25,678 --> 00:00:27,991
So what makes it different?

13
00:00:27,991 --> 00:00:31,411
It's the soft inner bark of the tree.

14
00:00:31,941 --> 00:00:34,752
Each stick is many paper-thin layers,

15
00:00:34,752 --> 00:00:36,271
rolled like a cigar.

16
00:00:36,271 --> 00:00:38,490
Cassia is one thick curl.

17
00:00:38,490 --> 00:00:40,779
It tastes sweeter and gentler,

18
00:00:40,779 --> 00:00:42,708
with a hint of citrus.

19
00:00:44,558 --> 00:00:46,138
But the biggest difference

20
00:00:46,138 --> 00:00:47,673
is hidden: coumarin.

21
00:00:47,673 --> 00:00:48,971
Cassia can carry

22
00:00:48,971 --> 00:00:50,756
around 100 times more.

23
00:00:50,756 --> 00:00:52,942
Ceylon has only traces.

24
00:00:52,942 --> 00:00:55,323
Too much can harm the liver:

25
00:00:55,323 --> 00:00:56,939
2 g of cassia a day

26
00:00:56,939 --> 00:00:59,315
hits Europe's safe limit.

27
00:00:59,845 --> 00:01:01,321
So how is it made?

28
00:01:01,321 --> 00:01:04,026
Twice a year, after the monsoons,

29
00:01:04,026 --> 00:01:05,834
new shoots are cut.

30
00:01:06,364 --> 00:01:08,657
A peeler scrapes the bark,

31
00:01:08,657 --> 00:01:10,861
rubs it with a brass rod,

32
00:01:10,861 --> 00:01:14,550
and lifts the inner layer in one piece.

33
00:01:15,080 --> 00:01:17,246
The strips are nested together

34
00:01:17,246 --> 00:01:20,023
and dried in the shade into quills.

35
00:01:20,553 --> 00:01:22,467
The finest grade, Alba,

36
00:01:22,467 --> 00:01:24,215
is under 6 mm across,

37
00:01:24,215 --> 00:01:26,782
about as thick as a pencil.

38
00:01:26,782 --> 00:01:28,763
Since 2022, Europe has

39
00:01:28,763 --> 00:01:30,723
protected the name.

40
00:01:31,253 --> 00:01:34,916
One island. One tree. Peeled by hand.
